WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.070
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.350 --> 01:24.080
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:29.880
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:31.390 --> 01:32.790
Brother...

01:32.860 --> 01:33.850
What is it?

01:33.930 --> 01:35.590
I'm kind of scared.

01:36.430 --> 01:38.450
I'm scared to go to our house.

01:46.910 --> 01:47.800
It's not here.

01:48.540 --> 01:50.240
Our house isn't here.

02:00.750 --> 02:02.050
<i>Connection</i>

02:02.050 --> 02:05.890
<i>Connection
Episode 6</i>

02:12.660 --> 02:14.130
What is the meaning of this?

02:14.870 --> 02:16.770
Why is our house gone?

02:29.310 --> 02:32.180
Where did our house go?

02:38.620 --> 02:39.650
Naoya...

02:51.470 --> 02:58.270
Today, we're making stew,
so I want you to help me a lot!

02:58.340 --> 03:01.340
Okay! Then I'll be in charge
of chopping the vegetables!

03:01.450 --> 03:04.040
Not allowed. It's too dangerous.

03:04.120 --> 03:05.640
You're in charge of washing.

03:05.720 --> 03:07.050
What, again?

03:08.120 --> 03:10.350
Okay! That's good, Naoto!

03:12.160 --> 03:14.390
Here it goes. Here!

03:15.830 --> 03:17.290
Hey, Dad!

03:17.360 --> 03:18.520
I'm sorry!

03:18.600 --> 03:19.930
Man!

03:21.570 --> 03:23.660
Mom that loved to cook...

03:24.340 --> 03:26.860
Dad that wasn't good at catch...

03:28.240 --> 03:30.230
Even if they erase our home...

03:30.310 --> 03:33.010
...they can't erase our memories too.

03:35.580 --> 03:37.410
What's wrong, Julia?

03:46.390 --> 03:48.290
Let me out of here!

03:50.000 --> 03:52.400
That streetlight is strange.

03:52.730 --> 03:57.600
Even if you put a new bulb in,
it goes out right away.

03:57.670 --> 04:01.830
It's creepy, so it's been
left like that for a long time.

04:03.440 --> 04:04.570
What?

04:04.710 --> 04:05.870
What's wrong?

04:11.450 --> 04:12.710
I researched it.

04:13.150 --> 04:16.250
This land has been empty
since a long time ago.

04:16.420 --> 04:17.650
There's no way!

04:17.720 --> 04:19.450
The dollhouse was still there!

04:19.520 --> 04:22.930
Also our memories,
and this streetlight!

04:24.230 --> 04:27.360
But there are no records
of it left anywhere.

04:27.970 --> 04:33.030
There is no proof anywhere
that this place was your home.

04:35.810 --> 04:38.470
Mr. Mikuriya sent me with a message.

04:38.540 --> 04:39.340
A message?

04:39.410 --> 04:43.870
He said if I wait here,
you guys would definitely show up.

04:46.650 --> 04:48.620
What did Mikuriya say?

04:51.960 --> 04:55.980
To find what you lost on your own...

04:56.730 --> 04:59.130
Find it on our own...

05:00.670 --> 05:01.500
Yes...

05:02.070 --> 05:03.660
Also, this...

05:03.970 --> 05:04.770
What's this?

05:04.770 --> 05:05.700
What's this?
Money.

05:21.320 --> 05:22.340
Hey...

05:23.360 --> 05:25.760
Do you remember me?

05:30.830 --> 05:32.560
I will contact you again.

05:33.000 --> 05:35.060
Please relay that to Mikuriya.

05:37.540 --> 05:38.700
Okay...

05:39.700 --> 05:40.730
Thank you...

05:41.910 --> 05:43.170
Good-bye.

05:56.890 --> 05:58.120
So bored...

05:58.820 --> 06:01.320
Why is it this boring?

06:02.130 --> 06:08.230
Hey, why do I have to keep on living
even though it's this boring?

06:17.310 --> 06:18.870
It's so boring...

06:19.910 --> 06:21.210
No!

06:21.280 --> 06:22.680
Why!

06:22.750 --> 06:24.010
Megumi!

06:24.220 --> 06:26.180
Why did you die!

06:26.350 --> 06:27.940
Megumi!

06:29.550 --> 06:31.250
C-Come on! What are you doing!

06:31.320 --> 06:34.720
Please stop! Please think
about our feelings also!

06:34.790 --> 06:37.560
Mother! Could we get a comment
on the whole suicide incident?

06:37.630 --> 06:38.990
Hey, mother!

06:39.100 --> 06:42.160
Of course the mass media is going to
cause a ruckus. It's the 3rd person.

06:42.230 --> 06:44.260
On top of that, they hung out together.

06:44.340 --> 06:47.100
Each week, one person before dawn.

06:47.170 --> 06:48.260
It makes me cringe.

06:48.340 --> 06:51.310
It's a curse. It's definitely a curse.

06:51.680 --> 06:53.770
Isn't it bad if they
don't have an exorcism?

06:53.850 --> 06:55.370
Who's next after Megumi?

06:55.450 --> 06:58.970
That's most likely the one that
Megumi was really good friends with.

07:08.730 --> 07:09.560
Yes...

07:11.730 --> 07:12.630
It's me.

07:15.830 --> 07:17.230
What is it?

07:17.570 --> 07:19.700
Just what did that mean?

07:19.940 --> 07:21.000
What's that?

07:21.310 --> 07:23.300
Why is our house gone?

07:23.440 --> 07:26.340
Did you do something
to our memories?

07:26.410 --> 07:28.540
I don't have that kind of power.

07:29.580 --> 07:32.570
If someone did something,
it was you guys.

07:33.320 --> 07:34.290
Us?

07:34.350 --> 07:36.480
That's what Mr. Misaki said.

07:37.020 --> 07:41.980
It seems your thoughts are
influencing what has happened.

07:42.290 --> 07:43.660
What do you mean?

07:43.730 --> 07:45.290
What is going on?

07:45.360 --> 07:48.130
Apparently, the axis of time
has been misaligned.

07:48.900 --> 07:50.930
The axis of time was misaligned?

07:51.000 --> 07:51.930
Yeah.

07:52.040 --> 07:53.500
That can't be.

07:56.740 --> 07:57.610
Is that true?

07:59.780 --> 08:00.870
Then...

08:01.780 --> 08:06.740
Then did our parents
disappear from this world?

08:06.820 --> 08:08.080
That's not possible.

08:08.150 --> 08:11.450
There is no way they
could have disappeared completely.

08:13.830 --> 08:17.630
Naoto, you have to find
the answer on your own.

08:17.700 --> 08:21.220
That's the message from Mr. Misaki.

08:24.870 --> 08:25.800
I have no business with you anymore.

08:25.800 --> 08:26.860
I have no business with you anymore.
Hold on a second.

08:27.870 --> 08:29.170
Do you know about the incident...

08:29.240 --> 08:32.440
...with students from the same
high school committing suicide?

08:32.780 --> 08:35.640
It's been reported in
a lot of different places.

08:36.480 --> 08:37.610
I don't know.

08:38.480 --> 08:40.080
I'm telling you to hold on.

08:55.330 --> 08:56.530
That's the spot.

08:59.640 --> 09:00.900
Let's go over there.

09:00.970 --> 09:01.840
Yeah.

09:06.950 --> 09:08.570
What's the matter, Naoya?

09:13.220 --> 09:14.450
Are you okay?

09:16.660 --> 09:17.640
Yeah...

09:21.530 --> 09:23.430
<i>Megumi</i>

09:46.790 --> 09:47.680
What's the matter?

09:47.950 --> 09:49.750
Get it together. Hey, Naoya!

09:50.220 --> 09:51.350
I'm okay...

10:00.230 --> 10:03.460
<i>Megumi</i>

10:11.410 --> 10:12.540
What's wrong, Naoya?

10:12.610 --> 10:13.410
Naoya!

10:16.680 --> 10:18.080
Hey, Naoya! Naoya!

10:18.320 --> 10:19.980
It's so boring...

10:22.490 --> 10:26.450
It's boring staying alive...

10:28.460 --> 10:29.890
Naoya! Naoya!

10:31.260 --> 10:33.060
I want to die...

10:40.870 --> 10:43.170
Wake up! You have
to wake up, Naoya!

10:46.280 --> 10:47.440
Brother...

10:50.750 --> 10:53.180
Don't align the
focal point more than this.

10:53.490 --> 10:54.880
You'll be taken over.

10:55.390 --> 10:56.180
Yeah.

11:04.230 --> 11:05.390
I can see...

11:06.700 --> 11:07.930
...the girl.

11:12.170 --> 11:14.100
There it goes! Run, run!

11:17.440 --> 11:18.470
Yeah!

11:19.110 --> 11:20.870
One person a week...

11:21.150 --> 11:24.210
The girl named Megumi
was the 3rd victim.

11:24.820 --> 11:28.780
It could be the result of
a spiritual occurrence.

11:28.850 --> 11:33.380
Meaning the first person that died
is inviting the next person?

11:33.460 --> 11:34.320
Yeah...

11:34.430 --> 11:39.390
I feel it's something spiritual
considering the fact they die at dawn.

11:39.560 --> 11:42.970
Spirits are still a type
of mental energy, so...

11:43.030 --> 11:47.160
But then we can't
do anything about it.

11:47.540 --> 11:51.740
Meaning Mikuriya also doesn't think
it's because of a spiritual existence.

11:56.980 --> 12:00.420
This town's air is muggy and heavy.

12:00.920 --> 12:03.080
Even I can tell that.

12:08.960 --> 12:10.090
Are you okay?

12:11.900 --> 12:13.590
Let's go to the school.

12:14.630 --> 12:15.620
Okay?

12:16.600 --> 12:17.570
Yeah...

12:33.550 --> 12:34.480
Hey!

12:34.950 --> 12:38.510
Can't you guys stay like a high
school student outside of school?

12:38.590 --> 12:40.680
That's why you guys are bad...

12:41.460 --> 12:43.980
Hey, Yanoguchi, stop.

12:48.800 --> 12:49.700
Yes?

12:50.940 --> 12:54.340
Man, what's with all that charm?

12:54.570 --> 12:56.100
What are you thinking?

12:57.310 --> 12:59.300
What the hell is this? A hickey?

12:59.380 --> 13:00.640
C-Come on!

13:00.710 --> 13:02.700
Man, Okita's doing it again.

13:02.780 --> 13:05.310
Oh man, poor Takiko...

13:07.790 --> 13:08.770
Idiot!

13:08.890 --> 13:11.580
She's so stuck up
because she's popular.

13:11.660 --> 13:12.990
Serves her right!

13:16.630 --> 13:17.750
Wh-What?

13:17.830 --> 13:19.490
What are you doing, you bastard!

13:20.370 --> 13:22.420
Oh, sorry, my foot slipped...

13:23.000 --> 13:24.490
Man, watch it!

13:24.570 --> 13:26.060
A hickey?

13:26.240 --> 13:29.000
Damn it, Takiko.
I wasn't the only one?

13:29.070 --> 13:32.240
She's hotter than
this ugly girl. Damn it!

13:32.310 --> 13:35.280
That girl... she played me!

13:35.350 --> 13:36.900
Serves her right!

13:36.980 --> 13:39.880
Takiko, she stole my boyfriend,
but she dumped him right way!

13:39.950 --> 13:42.720
Don't be stuck up
just because you're a little pretty!

13:42.790 --> 13:44.810
Nasty girl, die!

13:45.390 --> 13:46.760
Please stop!

13:47.560 --> 13:48.680
What's going on?

13:49.330 --> 13:50.450
What's the matter?

13:55.500 --> 14:02.170
Everyone thought of that girl at once,
so the thoughts got stronger.

14:02.240 --> 14:03.830
Hey, are you okay?

14:07.680 --> 14:08.840
What's going on?

14:08.910 --> 14:10.470
Miss Yamashita...

14:10.550 --> 14:13.520
Well, this boy just
sat down all of a sudden.

14:13.580 --> 14:15.640
He just started not
feeling well all of a sudden.

14:15.720 --> 14:16.620
It's nothing.

14:16.690 --> 14:17.380
Hold on!

14:37.640 --> 14:38.440
Let go of me!

14:40.910 --> 14:42.610
What was that just now?

14:42.680 --> 14:44.270
Get it together, Naoya.

14:44.350 --> 14:45.540
Hold on a second.

14:46.320 --> 14:48.750
Look, you have a fever!

14:48.950 --> 14:50.580
Rest a bit in the nurse's office.

14:55.930 --> 14:57.090
What the hell are you doing!

14:57.160 --> 15:00.460
Yeah! Yamashita was
concerned about you!

15:02.100 --> 15:03.070
Help!

15:03.130 --> 15:04.500
Brother, help me!

15:04.570 --> 15:06.500
Here, it's okay.

15:06.570 --> 15:07.370
Let's go.

15:07.940 --> 15:09.800
What's up with those guys?

15:15.080 --> 15:19.740
When humans gather together,
the minus consciousness expands.

15:20.390 --> 15:23.950
For us, it's impossible to go in there.

15:25.260 --> 15:29.750
People should have a lot of
plus consciousness too, though.

15:29.990 --> 15:31.480
I wonder why...

15:31.660 --> 15:33.890
An incident like that has happened.

15:34.200 --> 15:38.290
In the mass just like a chaining, the
minus consciousness is expanding...

15:38.370 --> 15:39.860
...so it's not strange.

15:51.220 --> 15:53.270
Brother, that girl...

15:53.350 --> 15:55.480
She's a friend of the girl who died.

16:02.630 --> 16:05.360
You're the friend of
the girl that died, right?

16:08.200 --> 16:09.960
The crystal pendant.

16:10.470 --> 16:12.630
The same one as Miss Megumi's...

16:12.970 --> 16:14.130
How?

16:14.510 --> 16:17.700
I didn't tell anyone about that.

16:20.980 --> 16:23.410
Could you tell us your story?

16:33.260 --> 16:35.190
Even though you say story...

16:35.260 --> 16:37.890
...we don't even
know what's going on.

16:38.460 --> 16:41.330
Well, we did talk
about it numerous times...

16:41.400 --> 16:44.230
...but no one comes to mind.

16:45.040 --> 16:47.560
I mean, isn't it weird? Three people.

16:47.870 --> 16:51.240
Three people committing suicide
one after another...

16:51.310 --> 16:52.400
This isn't possible.

16:53.310 --> 16:57.840
Even though Megumi said
she definitely wouldn't die...

17:01.390 --> 17:04.350
There's definitely nothing
that comes to your mind?

17:04.760 --> 17:06.350
There's nothing!

17:06.820 --> 17:09.620
Suicides and murder...

17:11.700 --> 17:13.130
I can't think of those.

17:17.000 --> 17:17.990
Hey...

17:18.970 --> 17:23.630
You think curses and
grudges actually exist?

17:24.180 --> 17:26.940
Is there something
that comes to your mind?

17:28.880 --> 17:31.080
There's no way that's possible.

17:32.150 --> 17:35.850
How did you guys
know about this pendant?

17:38.720 --> 17:42.660
The crystal's energy is unique,
so it's easy to catch.

17:43.090 --> 17:44.490
I don't understand.

17:44.660 --> 17:47.060
You guys are stranger.

17:47.870 --> 17:49.730
What kind of person is Mr. Okita?

17:50.430 --> 17:51.370
Horrible...

17:51.500 --> 17:53.060
Sexual harassment teacher...

17:53.600 --> 17:56.940
Masaki, who died,
was expelled because of him.

17:57.180 --> 17:58.270
Why was he expelled?

17:59.010 --> 18:01.310
When money disappeared
from the school...

18:01.380 --> 18:03.850
...he said that Masaki
was the one that did it.

18:04.280 --> 18:05.770
It definitely wasn't him.

18:06.280 --> 18:07.510
That's horrible.

18:08.390 --> 18:10.650
What about that Takiko girl?

18:10.720 --> 18:11.690
I hate her.

18:11.760 --> 18:12.620
Why?

18:12.690 --> 18:14.750
She's such a two-face...

18:15.130 --> 18:18.820
She's popular.
She changes guys left and right.

18:19.260 --> 18:23.890
Megumi said that the
only one Takiko likes is herself.

18:24.240 --> 18:26.400
Was she on bad terms
with Miss Megumi?

18:27.440 --> 18:30.430
Takiko went after Megumi's boyfriend.

18:30.940 --> 18:32.410
Then he dumped her.

18:32.710 --> 18:36.670
Since then, Takiko became
somewhat conscious about Megumi.

18:37.280 --> 18:40.440
Then what about the
health teacher, Miss Yamashita.

18:40.690 --> 18:42.050
She's a good teacher.

18:42.190 --> 18:43.740
She's really nice.

18:44.020 --> 18:46.790
Why do you ask
about Miss Yamashita?

18:47.760 --> 18:49.520
Could she have fought with someone...

18:49.590 --> 18:51.590
...or is someone holding
a grudge against her?

18:52.030 --> 18:56.360
But even if there were guys
holding a grudge like that...

18:56.430 --> 18:58.230
...how could they kill?

18:58.640 --> 19:00.800
I mean, it's all suicide.

19:03.470 --> 19:04.770
It was suicide.

19:05.780 --> 19:08.640
Why did you bring people
not part of us here?

19:08.910 --> 19:11.850
Didn't we say don't
bring anyone here ever?

19:12.120 --> 19:13.140
But...

19:13.250 --> 19:15.580
Three of your friends
are already dead, right?

19:15.650 --> 19:17.550
Isn't there something
that comes to your mind...

19:17.920 --> 19:20.150
There isn't!

19:20.220 --> 19:22.590
Freaking pretending
you're a nice person...

19:22.660 --> 19:25.220
Your true intentions are to sell
this information to somewhere, right?

19:25.300 --> 19:26.630
No, we're...

19:26.900 --> 19:28.590
We're telling you to leave!

19:28.670 --> 19:30.570
Brother, let's go, okay?

19:30.640 --> 19:31.970
Y-Yeah...

19:42.750 --> 19:45.340
That girl really
doesn't know anything.

19:45.820 --> 19:49.840
Her sadness has been numbed
from the shock of losing her friend.

19:50.320 --> 19:51.810
That's unavoidable...

19:53.290 --> 19:55.820
Naoya, what did you
find out at the school?

19:56.390 --> 19:59.850
That teacher named
Okita is a horrible person.

19:59.960 --> 20:06.060
But, the one that was the scariest was
that health teacher, Miss Yamashita.

20:06.340 --> 20:07.530
What did you see?

20:09.370 --> 20:10.270
Help!

20:10.410 --> 20:11.970
Brother, help me!

20:12.980 --> 20:14.640
The students were...

20:14.850 --> 20:17.010
She was slicing away at the students.

20:18.350 --> 20:21.550
She's always so nice
on the outside, so...

20:21.620 --> 20:24.820
...that's backlashing and
everything is piling up inside.

20:25.120 --> 20:29.250
The truth is there are
many students she hates.

20:29.830 --> 20:34.630
If the person isn't
aware of their dark side...

20:34.700 --> 20:40.640
...the desire that has been
held in grows pretty large...

20:41.210 --> 20:42.370
Brother...

20:43.140 --> 20:45.170
Miss Yamashita is scary.

20:45.510 --> 20:47.370
She's really scary.

21:02.330 --> 21:03.290
Yeah...

21:04.100 --> 21:05.490
The usual place.

21:05.600 --> 21:07.960
I should be able to
get there in like 10 minutes.

21:10.200 --> 21:14.900
Even though you say that, you're
always the one that comes later.

21:15.510 --> 21:17.770
What? I feel bad for your boyfriend.

21:17.840 --> 21:21.840
He denied Takiko's offer, right?
You have to value him.

21:23.980 --> 21:26.580
I know! Let's invite Masaki
and the others too!

21:26.650 --> 21:29.590
Then let's go hang out...

21:30.450 --> 21:31.220
...with...

21:31.220 --> 21:33.660
...with...
The number you have dialed...

21:33.720 --> 21:34.060
is no longer in use.

21:34.060 --> 21:35.420
...everybody...
...is no longer in use.

21:35.490 --> 21:38.360
Please check the
number and call back.

21:43.970 --> 21:45.130
Hey...

21:45.200 --> 21:47.000
Why are you crying?

21:48.610 --> 21:50.770
Why are you suffering?

21:51.780 --> 21:53.510
M-Megumi?

21:53.710 --> 21:55.440
Why are you lonely?

21:55.880 --> 21:58.510
Come on, let's go hang out!

21:58.580 --> 22:00.610
It's about 10 minutes past now!

22:01.220 --> 22:02.780
I got tired of waiting.

22:02.850 --> 22:04.620
Come on, let's go.

22:05.520 --> 22:06.580
Here...

22:06.920 --> 22:07.980
Come...

22:09.090 --> 22:10.290
...Yoshimi.

22:10.930 --> 22:12.400
Come...

22:15.370 --> 22:16.560
Yeah...

22:17.740 --> 22:20.670
No, don't pull me that much!

22:21.870 --> 22:22.900
Megumi!

22:29.910 --> 22:38.720
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:47.560
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

22:47.630 --> 22:56.400
<i>A single shadow looked like light
in this world that I'm imprisoned in.</i>

22:56.470 --> 23:05.210
<i>The rain of May became lighter
as it was kindly shining tomorrow.</i>

23:05.280 --> 23:09.620
<i>I lost the meaning of smiling...</i>

23:09.690 --> 23:13.990
<i>... that day I thought I
lost my place to be.</i>

23:14.060 --> 23:18.430
<i>I wished for your warmth.</i>

23:18.500 --> 23:22.930
<i>We have stopped time.</i>

23:23.170 --> 23:27.260
<i>I had this feeling it was
eventually going to come, but...</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:31.900
<i>... I pretended I didn't know
and buried my loneliness.</i>

23:31.980 --> 23:42.080
<i>I looked down at your feet as the
droplets describing "Good-bye" fell.</i>

23:42.720 --> 23:51.460
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

23:51.530 --> 23:59.900
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

24:02.110 --> 24:05.080
The wave of destruction that comes...

24:05.140 --> 24:07.340
...maneuvering into
the space of the heart.

24:07.410 --> 24:10.440
A small tragedy that
was hidden behind...

24:10.510 --> 24:12.280
...the enforcement
that is like the devil.

24:12.980 --> 24:17.110
